<section n="1" image-layout="right" id="9xon2oz6loyrf2d">
<img query="modern office with glowing screens and people working alongside digital AI interfaces, soft blue ambient light" ai-parsed-attrs="{&quot;loadImageParams&quot;:{&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;aiGenerated&quot;,&quot;query&quot;:&quot;modern office with glowing screens and people working alongside digital AI interfaces, soft blue ambient light&quot;,&quot;options&quot;:{&quot;aspectRatio&quot;:&quot;portrait&quot;,&quot;model&quot;:&quot;flux-1-quick&quot;,&quot;stylePrompt&quot;:&quot;Classy and modern with a corporate and minimalist touch. Tone is serious yet elegant, using a palette of light, white, and cool gray colors.&quot;,&quot;stylePreset&quot;:&quot;Theme&quot;,&quot;artStylePreset&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;artStylePrompt&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;styleReferenceImages&quot;:[],&quot;visualsMenuEnabled&quot;:false,&quot;styleReferenceKey&quot;:&quot;narrative_illustration&quot;}},&quot;source&quot;:&quot;image.ai-generated&quot;,&quot;loadImageStatus&quot;:&quot;queued&quot;,&quot;loadImageId&quot;:&quot;M0cRd&quot;}" class="accent-image">


<div class="body">
<h1>AI &amp; the Labor Market: Is AI Disrupting the Future of Work?</h1>
<p>A structured look at exposure, adoption, and what the evidence actually says.</p></div></section>

<section n="2" image-layout="blank" id="3m0iq4gr11w117v">



<div class="body"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/VMSOvYY9Zfap-mZNFpbQI.png" meta="null" resize="null" source="image.custom">
<h1>The Debate Is Real — and the Stakes Are Enormous</h1>
<smart-layout variant="stats">
<smart-layout-item number="$31T">
<h4>U.S. Economy</h4>
<p>Nearly 60% is labor costs — even a small AI shift moves <b>trillions</b> of dollars.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item number="300M">
<h4>Jobs at Risk Globally</h4>
<p>Roughly 27% of OECD positions could be transformed through AI automation.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item number="71%">
<h4>Americans Concerned</h4>
<p>Worry AI will put too many people out of work permanently — but the reality is more nuanced.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
</smart-layout></div></section>

<section n="3" image-layout="blank" id="l0juj5jrx77x8by">


<div class="body">
<h1>A Job Is a Bundle of Tasks — Not a Single Thing</h1>
<columns colWidths="[65,35]">
<div verticalAlign="center">
<img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/MfIJj4MZa3u3zYdmzsCic.png" meta="null" resize="null" shape="landscape" align="center" source="image.custom">
</div>
<div verticalAlign="center">
<p>AI almost never wipes out whole jobs overnight. It affects <b>tasks first</b> — some get automated, some get supercharged, some create entirely new work.</p>
<p>A doctor diagnoses, orders tests, interprets results, and coordinates care. A lawyer drafts, researches, argues, and advises. <b>Each task has a different AI exposure profile.</b></p>
<aside variant="info">The key insight: decompose the job into its tasks before assessing AI's true impact.</aside>
</div>
</columns></div></section>

<section n="4" image-layout="blank" id="j1oacx5cdqkfe37">


<div class="body">
<h1>A Three-Layer Framework for Understanding AI's Impact</h1>
<columns colWidths="[65,35]">
<div verticalAlign="center">
<img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/tcJaZfVcfO2bxZF3Nbfe_.png" meta="null" resize="null" shape="landscape" align="center" source="image.custom">
</div>
<div verticalAlign="center">
<smart-layout variant="outlineBoxesWithLabel" numbered="true" cellsize="10" cellSize="10">
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>Exposure</h4>
<p>Which tasks can AI plausibly assist or perform today?</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>Adoption</h4>
<p>How quickly will organizations actually deploy AI?</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>Labor Market Response</h4>
<p>Net effect on employment, wages, and new job creation.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
</smart-layout>
<p>These layers constantly feed back into each other — which is why the debate is so contentious.</p>
</div>
</columns></div></section>

<section n="5" image-layout="blank" id="4t5hmafiewbgvqy">


<div class="body">
<h1>Layer 1: Who Is Most Exposed?</h1>
<columns colWidths="[35,65]">
<div verticalAlign="center">
<h4>Highest Exposure</h4>
<p>Text-heavy, information-processing roles: legal research, financial analysis, programming, writing, customer support. High-paying, highly educated jobs score highest because their work is <b>language and symbol dense</b> — a reversal from earlier tech waves that automated routine physical tasks.</p>
<h4>Lowest Exposure</h4>
<p>Embodied, on-site, and interpersonal roles: electricians, roofers, nursing assistants, athletes. Physical manipulation and rich social interaction remain largely AI-resistant today.</p>
</div>
<div verticalAlign="center">
<img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/YUa98dwaWODFnA99ey7mK.png" meta="null" resize="null" shape="landscape" align="center" source="image.custom">
</div>
</columns></div></section>

<section n="6" image-layout="blank" id="2xvvt4auvddyx8k">


<div class="body">
<h1>AI Capabilities Are Racing Ahead of Expectations</h1>
<columns colWidths="[65,35]">
<div verticalAlign="center">
<img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/0EOfYbjRCdmBrLzAIiyt-.png" meta="null" resize="null" shape="landscape" align="center" source="image.custom">
</div>
<div verticalAlign="center">
<p>By 2024, AI surpassed the human baseline on reading comprehension, visual reasoning, PhD-level science questions, and multimodal understanding.</p>
<p>Researchers now describe a <b>"New Moore's Law"</b>: AI's autonomous task capacity doubles every ~7 months.</p>

</div>
</columns>
<smart-layout variant="minimalTimeline" orientation="vertical">
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>2026</h4>
<p>Completes a 2-hour task autonomously</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>2027</h4>
<p>Completes a full work day (8 hours)</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>2028</h4>
<p>Completes a full work week (40 hours)</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>2029</h4>
<p>Completes a full work month (167 hours)</p>
</smart-layout-item>
</smart-layout></div></section>

<section n="7" image-layout="blank" id="ans1hhdxu4mmt7d">




<div class="body">
<h1>Layer 2: Exposure ≠ Adoption</h1><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/36dqHYHpPqMq2xGj1uh38.png" meta="null" resize="null" source="image.custom">
<p>A job can be highly exposed in theory but untouched in practice. Legal constraints, union rules, data confidentiality, and workflow inertia all slow deployment.</p>
<smart-layout variant="solidJoinedBoxes">
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>54.6%</h4>
<p>Overall adult Gen AI adoption by August 2025 — up <b>10 points in a single year</b></p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>37.4%</h4>
<p>Work-specific adoption — still trailing personal use by a significant margin</p>
</smart-layout-item>
</smart-layout></div></section>

<section n="8" image-layout="blank" id="s58zyyawecz8q8t">


<div class="body">
<h1>The Productivity J-Curve: Why Gains Take Time</h1>
<columns colWidths="[65,35]">
<div verticalAlign="center">
<img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/q-WW-hRgYtpndVD52_C_A.png" meta="null" resize="null" shape="landscape" align="center" source="image.custom">
</div>
<div verticalAlign="center">
<p>Like electricity and the PC before it, AI is a <b>general-purpose technology</b>. The PC's productivity gains only appeared in U.S. statistics in the mid-1990s — 15 years after launch — as complementary software, networking, and new work practices matured.</p>
<aside variant="warning">A 2025 Harvard Business Review study found 40% of knowledge workers spend nearly <b>2 hours per week</b> fixing low-quality AI outputs — a real productivity drag before workflows mature.</aside>
</div>
</columns></div></section>

<section n="9" image-layout="left" id="hmzuy0kr6zfpxt8">
<img query="professional worker at a bright desk collaborating with AI dashboard on screen, confident and productive atmosphere" ai-parsed-attrs="{&quot;loadImageParams&quot;:{&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;aiGenerated&quot;,&quot;query&quot;:&quot;professional worker at a bright desk collaborating with AI dashboard on screen, confident and productive atmosphere&quot;,&quot;options&quot;:{&quot;aspectRatio&quot;:&quot;portrait&quot;,&quot;model&quot;:&quot;flux-1-quick&quot;,&quot;stylePrompt&quot;:&quot;Classy and modern with a corporate and minimalist touch. Tone is serious yet elegant, using a palette of light, white, and cool gray colors.&quot;,&quot;stylePreset&quot;:&quot;Theme&quot;,&quot;artStylePreset&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;artStylePrompt&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;styleReferenceImages&quot;:[],&quot;visualsMenuEnabled&quot;:false,&quot;styleReferenceKey&quot;:&quot;narrative_illustration&quot;}},&quot;source&quot;:&quot;image.ai-generated&quot;,&quot;loadImageStatus&quot;:&quot;queued&quot;,&quot;loadImageId&quot;:&quot;GqxrL&quot;}" class="accent-image">


<div class="body">
<h1>Response 1: Augmentation — AI Makes Workers More Productive</h1>
<smart-layout variant="solidBoxes" orientation="vertical" twoSided="false">
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>41% vs. 26%</h4>
<p>Daily AI users rating their productivity "Very Good" compared to non-users — plus measurable gains in focus, stress management, and job satisfaction.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>The Radiology Lesson</h4>
<p>Geoff Hinton predicted radiologists replaced within 5 years (2016). AI did outperform on benchmarks — but the field kept growing. Exposure and replacement are not the same thing.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
</smart-layout></div></section>

<section n="10" image-layout="blank" id="1gx83z0qbnntz0h">


<div class="body">
<h1>Response 2: Displacement — Real, But Concentrated</h1>
<columns colWidths="[35,65]">
<div verticalAlign="center">
<p>Clerical and back-office roles face the highest displacement risk: routine document processing, booking, transcription, and standardized communications are repeatedly flagged as highly automatable.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>"Look for jobs that are repetitive, independent, closed, short, forgiving, and digital — those are the ones most at risk on shorter timescales." — Andrej Karpathy</p>
</blockquote>
</div>
<div verticalAlign="center">
<img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/bbGVZndFwjHmGLZpma0Bu.png" meta="null" resize="null" shape="landscape" align="center" source="image.custom">
</div>
</columns></div></section>

<section n="11" image-layout="right" id="72bqwrqwd1k106x">
<img query="workers transitioning to new digital roles in a bright modern workspace, collaborative and optimistic tone" ai-parsed-attrs="{&quot;loadImageParams&quot;:{&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;aiGenerated&quot;,&quot;query&quot;:&quot;workers transitioning to new digital roles in a bright modern workspace, collaborative and optimistic tone&quot;,&quot;options&quot;:{&quot;aspectRatio&quot;:&quot;portrait&quot;,&quot;model&quot;:&quot;flux-1-quick&quot;,&quot;stylePrompt&quot;:&quot;Classy and modern with a corporate and minimalist touch. Tone is serious yet elegant, using a palette of light, white, and cool gray colors.&quot;,&quot;stylePreset&quot;:&quot;Theme&quot;,&quot;artStylePreset&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;artStylePrompt&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;styleReferenceImages&quot;:[],&quot;visualsMenuEnabled&quot;:false,&quot;styleReferenceKey&quot;:&quot;narrative_illustration&quot;}},&quot;source&quot;:&quot;image.ai-generated&quot;,&quot;loadImageStatus&quot;:&quot;queued&quot;,&quot;loadImageId&quot;:&quot;s7rB3&quot;}" class="accent-image">


<div class="body">
<h1>Response 3: Reinstatement — AI Creates New Roles Too</h1>
<smart-layout variant="arrowBullets" orientation="vertical" twoSided="false">
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>History Rhymes</h4>
<p>The PC era created software engineers, IT support, and digital marketers that didn't exist before. Technology revolutions rarely destroy jobs in aggregate — they transform them.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>New AI-Era Occupations</h4>
<p>AI engineers, prompt specialists, AI trainers, and trust &amp; safety roles are already emerging. Productivity gains lower costs, raise demand, and expand existing occupations.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>The Real Challenge</h4>
<p>The <b>pace and distribution</b> of change — who adapts fastest and who benefits most — will determine whether this transition is broadly shared or deeply unequal.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
</smart-layout></div></section>

<section n="12" image-layout="blank" id="l7466ybzv0pecwp">


<div class="body">
<h1>What to Watch: Three Questions That Will Determine the Outcome</h1>
<columns colWidths="[65,35]">
<div verticalAlign="center">
<img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/acme/uploaded-images/9yfLWL3zkz5f1WStGFzWZ.png" meta="null" resize="null" shape="landscape" align="center" source="image.custom">
</div>
<div verticalAlign="center">
<smart-layout variant="outlineBoxesWithSideLine" cellsize="10" cellSize="10">
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>Will adoption accelerate or plateau?</h4>
<p>If AI capability doubles every 4–7 months, the window for workers and institutions to adapt narrows dramatically.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>Who captures the productivity gains?</h4>
<p>Higher-wage, higher-educated workers are most exposed — and most positioned to benefit. Lower-wage workers face less disruption but fewer gains.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
<smart-layout-item>
<h4>How will policy respond?</h4>
<p>Retraining, labor protections, and safety nets will shape whether AI's abundance is broadly shared or concentrated at the top.</p>
</smart-layout-item>
</smart-layout>
</div>
</columns></div></section>

<section n="13" image-layout="blank" id="ghnwu8jgzlgm0jz">


